This is an independent implementation of the SAE J2534-1 PassThru API for the
Tactrix OpenPort 2.0. It is not derived from any prior codebase.

The wire protocol it speaks was established by observing a physical OpenPort
2.0 (firmware 1.17.4877) and is documented in docs/PROTOCOL.md. The J2534-1
constants, structure layouts and function signatures are those of the SAE
standard, which is what makes any J2534 library interchangeable with another.

Interoperability sources. To establish what the cable accepts and how its
replies are meant to be read, the vendor's own Windows driver was run as a
black box and its traffic compared with this driver's (tools/ab-official),
and the header and sample programs that ship in the vendor's public driver
installer were read for interface constants and observable behaviour. No
vendor code was copied, and no vendor binary was disassembled or decompiled.

